From: mcc45tr <mcc45tr@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 17:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] libssc: fix public property value types

The stream-type, available and sample-rate getters return guint, gboolean and
gfloat respectively, but their GParamSpecs incorrectly declare strings.  A
typed g_object_get() therefore triggers GLib criticals and can overwrite a
caller's scalar with a pointer-sized value.

Declare the ABI's actual value types.  Property names and access flags remain
unchanged, so existing clients which use the documented scalar values continue
to work while generic SSC monitors can inspect stream policy safely.

Signed-off-by: mcc45tr <mcc45tr@gmail.com>
---
 src/libssc-sensor.c | 17 +++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/libssc-sensor.c b/src/libssc-sensor.c
index c50a60d..4e2557f 100644
--- a/src/libssc-sensor.c
+++ b/src/libssc-sensor.c
@@ -890,6 +890,8 @@ ssc_sensor_class_init (SSCSensorClass *klass)
 	properties[PROP_STREAM_TYPE] =
-		g_param_spec_string (SSC_SENSOR_STREAM_TYPE,
+		g_param_spec_uint (SSC_SENSOR_STREAM_TYPE,
 				     "Stream type",
 				     "The stream type supported by the sensor.",
-				     NULL,
+				     0,
+				     G_MAXUINT,
+				     0,
 				     G_PARAM_READABLE);
@@ -898,6 +900,6 @@ ssc_sensor_class_init (SSCSensorClass *klass)
 	properties[PROP_AVAILABLE] =
-		g_param_spec_string (SSC_SENSOR_AVAILABLE,
+		g_param_spec_boolean (SSC_SENSOR_AVAILABLE,
 				     "Availability",
 				     "If the sensor is available for measurements.",
-				     NULL,
+				     FALSE,
 				     G_PARAM_READABLE);
@@ -906,6 +908,8 @@ ssc_sensor_class_init (SSCSensorClass *klass)
 	properties[PROP_SAMPLE_RATE] =
-		g_param_spec_string (SSC_SENSOR_SAMPLE_RATE,
+		g_param_spec_float (SSC_SENSOR_SAMPLE_RATE,
 				     "Sample rate",
 				     "The sample rate in Hz supported by the sensor.",
-				     NULL,
+				     -G_MAXFLOAT,
+				     G_MAXFLOAT,
+				     0.0f,
 				     G_PARAM_READABLE);
-- 
